I think I was never a ghost in my own room.

When I bowed my head, I chose the angle of the light.

When hands rested on the small of my back,

I think I must've paved the road that brought them there.

Call it devotion. Or a trade..I’m not sure.

I liked the gravity of a heavier shadow,

like into a play I thought someone else wrote,

playing the fragile thing, the porcelain hinge,

only because my finger was already tracing the lock.

Was every meekness just a quiet architecture?

Every yield, a domain I mapped before footprint ever met the floor.

Q
